    "narrative": "The Ghost Ride the WHIP lineup hinges on two high-leverage outfielders today, headlined by **James Wood**, who commands the day\u2019s highest score at 74.79. Facing Sandy Alcantara, **Wood** benefits from the opposition\u2019s slow delivery (88% SB conversion rate), making him our primary engine for both speed and offensive production. **Corbin Carroll** follows closely with a 61.26 rating; while he faces a tougher matchup against Emmet Sheehan, his ability to manufacture stolen bases and high xwOBA metrics make him a \"must-start\" despite the difficult SP_xERA of 3.21. **Vinnie Pasquantino** remains a rock-solid play at 56.70, largely driven by a strong platoon advantage against Richardson, which helps mitigate the threat of a sub-3.00 xERA pitcher.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Cole Young**, who fell just short of our 40-point start threshold with a 38.68 score. While **Young** provides necessary depth, the combination of a middling park factor and the current SP_xERA of 3.59 for Austin Warren kept him on the pine to protect our daily game caps. Meanwhile, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Dalton Rushing**, **Gabriel Moreno**, **Brice Turang**, and **Kyle Karros**, as their slots are currently listed as \"Lineup Pending.\" Should **Turang** or **Rushing** be bumped down the order or scratched, we will need to pivot quickly. We remain diligent about the risks posed by elite arms like those of Sheehan, though we are comfortable leaning into the speed profiles of **Wood** and **Carroll** to keep our SB category competitive in today\u2019s 5x5 slate.",
